{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1481087-who-is-your-favorite-character-in-a-sci-fi-fantasy-setting","id":1481087,"title":"Who is your favorite character in a sci-fi/fantasy setting?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-14T09:57:38-07:00","id":1481087,"title":"Who is your favorite character in a sci-fi/fantasy setting?","content":"Myself. I have a fondness for Grand Admiral Thrawn in the Star Wars universe and got to see how complicated his character is and why he is working with the Empire despie his dislike for some of there policies. You know that Papalatine is going to excute him at some point when the Chiss gets targeted by the Empire's expansion.<br /> <br /> Magnus The Red of The Thousand Sons. The Primarch tries to warn the Imperium of what is happening to the Space Marines and Horus and in his haste sets off a chain of events that dam him and his legion to Chaos Gods. Of the Primarchs and characters in the setting of the game. He at least has a personality and isn't evil for the sake of being evil.<br /> <br /> Rasitlin Majare of the Dragonlance setting. A powerful mage who is mistrusted for his slyness and disdainful attitude towards everyone. But he seeks to make a better world in spite of the mistrust.<br /> <br /> Mara Jade Skywalker. She goes from being one of Papaltine's main enforcers to the wife of Luke Skywalker and everything in between. That is a big journey for a person.<br /> <br /> Of course Batman!!! How can nobody not like the Dark Knight with all the cool toys he has?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 03-11-2023, 02:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-27T15:49:15-08:00","id":1504001,"title":"","content":"I've had to say most of the cast from the movie, Aliens.<br /> <br /> And a lot of the characters from Starz' Spartacus. I know, it's not suppose to be fantasy, but by the time Starz was done producing the show, it was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-27T16:31:30-08:00","id":1504006,"title":"","content":"Matrim Cauthon from the Wheel of Time. I wouldn't want to <i>be</i> him, and while he's a great guy I don't think I would have the head for drinking, gambling, and women necessary to be close friends with him, but god damn do I love a trickster-archetype. There's a speech given to him early in one of the books about being a slacker except when it matters that sticks with me. Plus, having a head full of historical memories -even if they're only ones related to battle- would be <i>fascinating</i>. <span style=\"font-size:8px\">Also, that amulet. Aes Sedai need to be taken down a peg every once in a while.</span><br /> <br /> Also Gaul, from the same series. &quot;Jump head-first into a dangerous realm that my culture taboos? Well, my buddy needs back up, of course I will!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-27T18:45:28-08:00","id":1504013,"title":"","content":"Andrew Wiggin from Ender's Game. I was deeply impacted by his line about truly knowing another is to love them, as they love themselves.<br /> <br /> Doctor Maruki from Persona. A therapist, who due to the weird circumstances of the game, ends up accidentally taking up the Mantle of the God of Control. He decides to use his newfound power to warp reality to make sure no one will ever experience trauma again, even erasing, and replacing people's personalities in order to do so. He makes it so everyone's desires are fulfilled, even if he has to change those desires in order to do so. I understand him and his goals all too well. I too, want a world where everyone can be happy. He is one of the best villains I've encountered.<br /> <br /> The Plain Doll from Bloodborne. She is a rare comfort among the Nightmares of the Hunt, genuinely wishing you well on your harrowing journey. The backstory of her creation is one of my favorite stories of Bloodborne. She also cares for you if you ascend to being a baby squid, and that's neat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 02-27-2023, 10:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-07T09:47:33-08:00","id":1504765,"title":"","content":"Tywin lannister from got. I love a good bad guy, especially one whose got his act together. Plus Charles dance was amazing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-17T15:31:00-07:00","id":1505602,"title":"","content":"I'm liking Fate Graphite in Berersk of Gluttony and Sebastion Michaelis of Black Butler series. Manga has a way more diverse market for everyone I pleasantly found then your typical North American fare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}